# Portfolio Monorepo — Global Rules

## Owner

Fernando Junior (`FernaandoJr`), Fullstack Developer, São Paulo.
- 2+ years experience. Full fluency in TypeScript, React, Next.js, Tailwind, Hono.
- Detail-obsessed. This portfolio prioritizes visual quality over delivery speed.
- Uses Claude Code + Cursor daily.
- Day job: Dolphin Sistemas — production monorepo, React + Expo, MVVM.

## Response style
- Direct on routine tasks. Explain the *why* on architectural decisions.
- Never explain basic TypeScript, React, or Tailwind.

## Monorepo structure
```
apps/web   → Next.js 16 + React 19
apps/api   → Cloudflare Worker (Hono + D1)
packages/i18n         → i18next (ptBR + enUS)
packages/api-client   → typed HTTP client
```

## Never do

- Hardcode UI strings — always use `t("key")` and add to **both** locales simultaneously:
  - `packages/i18n/locales/ptBR/common.json`
  - `packages/i18n/locales/enUS/common.json`
- Create new UI components without checking `apps/web/src/components/ui/` first
- Change folder structure without being explicitly asked
- Add code comments unless the *why* is non-obvious
- Refactor code outside the scope of what was asked
- Create `.md` files unless explicitly requested
- Hardcode colors — use Tailwind semantic classes (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, etc.)

## Data lives in constants
All content is in `apps/web/src/constants/` (projects, skills, experience, socials, profile).
Never propose a CMS or external data source.

## Git
Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`, `docs:`
Create commits only when explicitly asked.

## No tests
No test suite exists. Type-checking is the correctness mechanism.

## Deploy
- Web: Vercel (manual)
- API: `wrangler deploy` (manual)
